            <div xml:id="d225">

                <pb facs="0448" n="374" sameAs="frus:frus1941-43/pg374"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Roosevelt Papers</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the President
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-12-29">December 29,
                        1941</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Memorandum for the
                    President</hi>:</p>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential and in haste</hi></p>
                <p>I enclose herewith the proposed amendment[s] to our Joint Declaration offered by
                    the Soviet Ambassador for his Government. The Soviet Ambassador tells me that
                    the word “Hitlerism” with his country includes Nazism, Fascism and Japanism, and
                    hence his Government may stick rather strongly for this word. I mention this so
                    you will have the full background. I see no particular objection to the other
                    proposals.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>C.H.</signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d225-a1.xml" xpointer="d225-a1"/>
